{"id":"h006","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Battle of Agincourt took place in 1066.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Battle of Agincourt was fought on 25 October 1415.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-2.7502},{"text":"Agincourt took place during the Hundred Years' War, with Henry V defeating a larger French army.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-2.7781},{"text":"1066 is the year of the Battle of Hastings, where William of Normandy defeated Harold Godwinson.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":3.0596},{"text":"Agincourt and Hastings are often confused and mentioned together in school history.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-1.6587},{"text":"The shared English involvement and the fame of 1066 make the mix-up plausible, so the claim might seem believable.","confidence":0.4,"lean":1,"theta":0.6283,"phi":-0.8174},{"text":"Contemporary chronicles and modern scholarship consistently date Agincourt to 1415.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-2.7756},{"text":"Hastings was a different battle about 350 years before Agincourt.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.5434},{"text":"The claim that Agincourt took place in 1066 is false.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-2.8583}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":6,"J":-0.5,"relatio